<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="81bc7a01">On large implementations, a Solution Architect oversees the work of the Functional Architects.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="e65963d"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="d3307b3d"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="4405f779">&lt;p&gt;
    The Solution Architect is typically responsible for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirming that the client&apos;s operational strategy is fully supported by the target state solution design
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirming that the project-specific business process design meets business needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Leading or overseeing the process design workshops
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identifying project-specific processes and functional gaps
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Overseeing the resolution of identified gaps and solution design issues
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Supporting project-specific planning and delivery of change activities
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
